ly hassles directly increases one's ability to navigate and understand larger spatial scales, as frequent problem-solving and adaptation to daily challenges might be thought to train the brain to process broader and more complex environments. Therefore, people who face more daily hassles could be falsely assumed to have improved spatial scale cognition.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.0022804399410223373, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7136573654328491, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.000982623863676923, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2974077075996135}

