   Properties: {'session_id': '1c6dbdd4-e443-478d-afb3-88270911794a', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5185442872491721, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9480680/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6086945/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10367528/', 'https://www.psychiatry.pitt.edu/sites/default/files/inline-files/PSQI%20Article.pdf', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4221412/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08962564041737182, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation provides a coherent causal chain: sleep disturbance leads to an adaptive reduction in basal metabolic rate, which reduces caloric expenditure and thus increases BMI. Each step is logically connected, and the overall reasoning is internally consistent. No major logical flaws or unsupported leaps are present in the argument as presented.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7188315298731215, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6947234243722425, 'motivation': 'Sleep disturbance (PSQI) leads to an increase in body mass index (BMI) by causing the body to conserve energy during waking hours. When individuals experience frequent sleep disturbances, their bodies adapt by lowering basal metabolic rate throughout the day to compensate for the perceived threat of insufficient rest. This adaptive metabolic slowdown directly results in reduced caloric expenditure, thereby contributing to increased BMI. Consequently, greater sleep disturbance is associated with higher BMI, as the body’s energy conservation response to disrupted sleep hinders effective weight management.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Sleep disturbance (PSQI) leads to an increase in body mass index (BMI) by causing the body to conserve energy during waking hours. When individuals experience