185. Proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6)-[POSITIVE]->Body mass index (BMI)
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1240780039514089, 'original_motivation': 'Proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) do not directly cause body mass index (BMI) to change. While BMI can influence proinflammatory markers, there is no established causal pathway where changes in proinflammatory processes directly alter BMI. Any association is likely mediated by other variables such as metabolic rate, physical activity, or adiposity, which are not direct effects.', 'session_id': '1c6dbdd4-e443-478d-afb3-88270911794a', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5785574895970438, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08534564935906194, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that increased proinflammatory processes directly cause higher BMI by stimulating fat cell growth and promoting weight gain, and that this effect occurs regardless of other factors. However, the reasoning is overly simplistic and fails to account for the complexity of the relationship. While inflammatory cytokines may influence fat metabolism, asserting a direct and inherent causality from inflammation to increased BMI, without considering additional mediating factors or the potential for reverse causality (i.e., higher BMI leading to higher inflammation), is logically unsound. The explanation overstates the directness and independence of the causal link.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6622848515220005, 'motivation': 'Increased proinflammatory processes, such as higher levels of TNF-alpha and IL-6, directly cause an increase in body mass index (BMI) by stimulating fat cell growth and promoting weight gain. This suggests that higher inflammation inherently makes people gain more body fat regardless of other factors.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increased proinflammatory processes, such as higher levels of TNF-alpha and IL-6, directly cause an increase in body mass index (BMI) by stimulating fat cell growth and promoting weight gain. This suggests that higher inflammation inherently makes people gain more body fat regardless of other factors.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.008756212681239618, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7474189668075997, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 9.304830918431103e-05, 'judge_prob_std': 0.292139777091484}

