   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.4912875632530818, 'original_motivation': 'Mindfulness (FFMQ) causes sleep disturbance (PSQI) to decrease in an inverse causal relationship. Increases in mindfulness are known to reduce sleep disturbances by promoting relaxation and reducing rumination. Conversely, decreases in mindfulness can lead to greater sleep disturbance. This relationship is not mediated by other variables present in the CLD.', 'session_id': '6bbcf614-8233-4ff4-accf-a252cd72bcb9', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8368088896276573, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.11076937727052202, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation asserts that higher mindfulness, as measured by the FFMQ, leads to increased rumination and heightened self-awareness, which in turn increases sensitivity to bodily sensations and thoughts at bedtime, thereby causing more sleep disturbances. Let\\u2019s break this down step by step:"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6300749921107821, 'motivation': 'Higher mindfulness, as measured by the FFMQ, can lead to increased rumination and heightened self-awareness, which may make individuals more sensitive to minor disruptions in their sleep. This increased attention to bodily sensations and thoughts at bedtime could exacerbate sleep disturbances, thus higher mindfulness would be associated with more sleep problems.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher mindfulness, as measured by the FFMQ, can lead to increased rumination and heightened self-awareness, which may make individuals more sensitive to minor disruptions in their sleep. This increased attention to bodily sensations and thoughts at bedtime could exacerbate sleep disturbances, thus higher mindfulness would be associa