 directly increase the likelihood of smoking. This relationship is widely supported in behavioral science literature as a direct causal pathway.', 'prob_std': 0.2898303763794882, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.4922857435342272, 'max_window_entropy': 1.0773891928713857}

