 anti-inflammatory cytokine, directly reduces inflammatory activity, which is known to improve sleep quality and decrease sleep disturbances. Conversely, decreased IL-10 can lead to increased inflammation and worsen sleep disturbance. The causal direction is from anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) to sleep disturbance (PSQI), not the reverse.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0, 'perplexity': 1.2506856921320668, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8566036078795134, 'min_prob': 0.11810028171057317, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7152117775121103, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00106416199388906, 'prob_variance': 0.056787870756320975, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0722967231994218, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0009982324341807458, 'judge_prob_std': 0.32144136616775126, 'avg_nll': 0.22369195461927854}

