ght be associated with increased proinflammatory processes.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "Practicing mindfulness often increases self-awareness, which can heighten an individual's sensitivity to bodily sensations, including minor aches and discomforts. This increased focus on internal states could potentially lead to higher stress reactivity, thereby stimulating greater production of proinflammatory cytokines such as TNF-alpha and IL-6. Therefore, higher mindfulness might be associated with increased proinflammatory processes.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.015488294610454709, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7189113244410745, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0033829746648708628, 'judge_prob_std': 0.31561871750030257}

