 sleep quality, as measured by lower PSQI scores, can paradoxically lead to an increase in depressive symptoms because individuals may spend more time in bed ruminating on negative thoughts. Thus, better sleep could actually worsen depressive symptoms, suggesting a negative association between sleep disturbance and depression.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7215112443173813, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0030635583078170467, 'judge_prob_std': 0.30930595107515785}

